<p>Fundis (masons, plumbers, electricians, carpenters and other tradespeople) bring customers to the shop. HardPoint keeps
  each fundi's commission for you: it's earned when a sale they brought is paid, taken back if it's voided or returned,
  and paid out in cash or by M-Pesa. Switch it on in <strong>Settings › Features › Fundi commissions</strong>.</p>

<h2>Setting the rates</h2>
<p>Go to <strong>Customers › Fundis › Commission rates</strong> (owners and managers). Set a <strong>shop rate</strong>, say 2%,
  then a different rate for any category where it differs: less on cement, more on fittings. A subcategory without a rate uses
  its parent's. Commission is worked on each line's value <strong>before tax</strong>. If you've agreed a rate with one fundi,
  put it on their page as <strong>their own rate</strong>; they get it on everything instead.</p>

<h2>Adding fundis</h2>
<p>Press <strong>New</strong> on <strong>Customers › Fundis</strong>, or <strong>New fundi</strong> from the till. Their phone
  number is the one you pay them on by M-Pesa. A fundi who has stopped coming can be made inactive; their history stays.</p>

<h2>Naming the fundi at the till</h2>
<p>Under the customer at the top of the sale, press <strong>Add</strong> beside <strong>Fundi</strong> and search by name or
  phone. A quote or order can name the fundi too, and collecting it at the till carries them to the sale. Nothing is earned until
  the sale is paid in full. Sales made on the offline till don't name a fundi.</p>

<h2>What they're owed, and paying them</h2>
<p>Each fundi's page is their statement: every sale they brought, anything taken back, every payment, and what's owed now.
  Owners and managers press <strong>Pay commission</strong> and choose <strong>M-Pesa</strong> (type the M-Pesa code) or
  <strong>Cash from a till</strong>: the cash is recorded as a payout from that till, so its count at close still balances, and
  the profit and loss counts it as an expense. You can't pay more than is owed.</p>

<h2>Reports and emails</h2>
<p><strong>Reports › Fundi commissions</strong> shows, for any period, what each fundi brought in, earned, had taken back and was
  paid, and what each is owed today. The Monday summary email lists the fundis who brought in the most that week.</p>
